LAIGO — LEGO Mosaic Builder
============================

Converts a photo into a LEGO mosaic: a color-quantized brick layout,
a Pick-a-Brick order list (uploadable to lego.com), and a step-by-step
PDF build guide. The finished build pack is sold pay-what-you-want
(name your price; $0 is allowed).

Full project guide: CLAUDE.md


Running locally
---------------

From the project root, in PowerShell:

    .venv\Scripts\activate.ps1
    uvicorn scripts.Main:app --reload

Open the Swagger UI at  http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

The server MUST be started from the project root with the
package-qualified path (`scripts.Main:app`) — `cd scripts; uvicorn Main:app`
fails because `Main.py` uses relative imports.


First-time setup
----------------

1. Create the venv and install deps (project root).
2. Copy `.env` (committed defaults) and create `.env.secrets` (gitignored).
   For the pay-what-you-want endpoints, set `STRIPE_SECRET_KEY` and
   `STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET` (see CLAUDE.md "Payment provider"). The default
   `DB_BACKEND=json` needs no database — there is nothing to migrate.

The automated checkout / marketplace-ordering pipeline is shelved; its setup
(marketplace API keys, Neon DB, alembic migrations) is only needed if you
re-enable it — see docs/BACKEND_SWITCHING.md and the SHELVED docs.


Basic usage
-----------

POST /generate              (multipart upload) — kicks off a mosaic job.
GET  /jobs/{job_id}                            — poll job status.
GET  /jobs/{job_id}/preview                    — 3D-renderable mosaic JSON (docs/PREVIEW_API.md).
GET  /jobs/{job_id}/download                   — download the artifact zip when complete (ungated).
POST /jobs/{job_id}/pay                         — pay-what-you-want charge for the build pack.
POST /donate                                   — standalone tip (client-confirm Stripe).

The zip contains:
  - order_list.json       (upload to lego.com Pick-a-Brick)
  - instructions.pdf      (step-by-step build guide)


Running the tests
-----------------

From project root (`.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m scripts.<name>`):

Live product:

    scripts.test_pay_router
    scripts.test_donate_router
    scripts.test_preview
    scripts.test_background_budget
    scripts.test_order_list
    scripts.test_piece_specs
    scripts.test_jobs_store_json
    scripts.test_jobs_store_edge

Shelved checkout pipeline (test_optimizer, test_gate_bypass,
test_saga_state_machine run with no DB; test_jobs_store_dispatch,
test_phase_e_pg, test_reconcile_pg, test_jsonb_codec need
DB_BACKEND=postgres + a Neon DSN).
